/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6ffbe589/D6/2/code.py:17:#    - The old output was one tight crop of the whole repaired board.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6ffbe589/D6/2/code.py:18:#    - The new output is a gallery: after repairing the board, isolate each color layer, tight-crop that
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6ffbe589/D6/2/code.py:19:#      single-color layer, then concatenate those crops left-to-right with one background column between frames.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6ffbe589/D6/2/code.py:21:#      old flow: crop whole board -> rotate blue/red/yellow masks in-place -> return NxN repaired crop.
